own":0.12487,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":83.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Space Exploration Technologies Corp. provides satellite-based broadband services in the United States, Ireland, Canada, and internationally. It operates through three operating segments: Space, Connectivity, and AI. The Space segment designs, manufactures, and launches reusable rockets to provide access to space. It also provides launch services for the deployment of payloads to intended orbits for commercial and government customers utilizing Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy; and engages in the launch and development for the development of spacecraft and the provision of launch and mission services for government agency space programs utilizing Falcon 9, Falcon Heavy, Starship, and Dragon. Its company's Connectivity segment operates broadband data and communications network by various Starlink satellites in low-earth orbit, delivering connectivity to various consumers, enterprise, and government customers. The company's AI segment operates a vertically integrated AI platform spanning a frontier LLM Grok; AI solutions for consumer and enterprise customers; X, a real-time information, entertainment, and free speech platform; and AI computational infrastructure. Space Exploration Technologies Corp. was incorporated in 2002 and is based in Starbase, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Elon R. Musk | Founder, Chairman, CTO & CEO | Age 54 | Compensation: $54,080 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 21K people. Revenue per employee of $889K ranks in the top quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $93K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). R&D investment of 46% of revenue (heavy) signals commitment to product development and talent.","financial_summary":["Space Exploration Technologies  is a mega-cap industrials business with a $1.9T market cap on $18.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +34% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 43%.","The company is burning through $14.1B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 0.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 12% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"SGA costs surged 46% YoY \u2014 may reflect legal, restructuring, or operational issues","sev":"red","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Operating margins 20% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 1091% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":10.905287009063445},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $53.7M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 6% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Growing faster than most Industrials peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","R&D investment (46% of revenue) is above Industrials peers, supporting innovation"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SpaceX (SPCX) Orders 100 GW Solar Line And Unveils $24 Billion Texas AI Hub","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/telecom/nasdaq-spcx/space-exploration-technologies/news/spacex-spcx-orders-100-gw-solar-line-and-unveils-24-billion","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794608934.625,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.599,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"SpaceX\u2019s Starship Just Did Something for Only the 2nd Time. Saturday Could Be Even Bigger.","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/spacex-starship-just-did-something-003501000.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794616734.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.052,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Here's What $1,000 in Each of These 3 Space Stocks Could Be Worth by 2030","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/artic